WEBVTT

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.850
Hello and welcome back.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:32.950
I'm glad you could join me today.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.390
I hope you've got your palette set up

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:35.890
and your almighty easel and you're ready

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.970
to paint a beautiful painting with me.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.270
Today I thought we'd do a little painting.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:42.050
It's just a lot of fun and I really think you'll enjoy it.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.850
I'm gonna have them graphically run all the colors

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.810
across the screen that we'll need to do the project today.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.430
These colors will come across your screen

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.330
in the same order that I have them on my palette,

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.110
starting with a white and working across.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.450
So, let's get started.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.950
I'm gonna start out today with a little bit

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.000
of alizarin crimson on the large brush, take a smaller

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.920
amount of paint out, tap it into the bristles.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.580
This assures a nice, even distribution of paint

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.200
all through the brush.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.800
Now, use very little paint.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.860
I'm gonna put this in the sky,

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.440
and I don't want to set the sky on fire.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.280
All I want to do is put a little pinkish glow into it.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.560
Okay, let's go up to the canvas here.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.510
Now, let's start right in here,

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.520
and we make little X's, little criss-cross.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.180
Now, the canvas has already been covered with Magic White,

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.450
good and wet and slick, and ready to go.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.350
Very easy to add more color.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.040
But it's the sun I'm gonna try to take it off,

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.400
so if you want more color, just pick it up and put it on.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.670
But start with very, very little color.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.380
I'll add a little tiny bit more right in here.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:48.640
There we go.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.140
Now while I've got that on the brush,

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:54.900
maybe right down in here with a little.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.950
Without cleaning the brush,

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:00.000
I'm gonna go right into a small amount of Prussian blue.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.200
Now the Prussian blue is very, very strong.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.740
Be careful with it.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:08.510
Little criss-cross.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:12.680
It will consume your crimson in a heartbeat,

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.910
so be careful with it.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.660
Very little Prussian blue.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.050
So, so strong.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:23.870
Once again, you can always add a little more if you want it,

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.510
but it's hard to take it off.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.370
If you ever do need to take it off,

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.000
you can take a clean, dry brush.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.640
brush and go over it and it'll pick up paint.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.600
Or if worse comes to worse, if it's really bad,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.360
you can take a paper towel or a clean rag

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:40.530
and just wipe the canvas down and start over.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.190
'Cause at this point, you really haven't invested

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:45.880
a lot of time or energy into your painting.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:53.080
Okay, and maybe I'll put just a tiny bit of blue

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.460
right here, I don't want much, just a little.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.200
Maybe there'll be a little water right there.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.700
We'll make that decision later.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.340
And I'm gonna clean the brush.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.260
And we clean the brush with odorless paint thinner.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:10.480
And there's a screen in the bottom of my can.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.670
Hey, hey.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.710
And we scrub the brush against the screen

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.830
and that takes the paint off.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.090
And allows the solid material to settle to the bottom

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.130
of the can and it doesn't contaminate

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.810
all your paint thinner.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.690
Okay, there we go.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.380
Gives us a nice little sky very quickly, very simply.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:30.000
A lot of fun.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.760
Let's go, let's go.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.150
Get us a big old fan brush.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.530
I'm gonna go into the titanium white

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.800
and load a lot of paint onto your brush.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.230
A lot of paint, pull it through there.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:47.520
And I'm gonna pick up a small amount of permanent red.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.090
Just a little bit, a little bit.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.840
It's very, very strong.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.710
Look at all the paints on that brush.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.830
There, let's go up to the canvas now.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.000
Let's build a happy little cloud and maybe he'll

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.530
lives right here.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:04.070
Now I'm just using the corner of the brush,

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:13.160
making tiny little circles, tiny little circles.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:17.140
Get a little more paint on my brush.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.300
You're looking for areas that have a lot of paint,

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:23.320
areas that have virtually no paint, thick, thin.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.190
Some areas you don't want to put anything on,

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.740
so it'll turn out to be your shadows.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.000
Now with a large brush,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.170
I'm gonna gently, gently blend this out.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:37.680
Just blend it, little tiny circles.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:43.120
Tiny little circles, there we go.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.580
Fluff it, just grab it and fluff it up.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:52.040
And then very gently blend it all together.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:55.350
Let's see, isn't that easy?

00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:00.000
It's a super way to make fantastic little clouds, very easy.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.020
Clouds used to give me a fit

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:12.010
until I found out how easy they were to make.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:17.180
This comes right on, wherever you want it, wherever.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:21.870
Still just titanium white.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.910
Okay, now we'll take our big brush again

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.080
and do the same thing.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.520
Blend the bottom out.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.100
We're not touching the top edge of the cloud yet at all.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.060
And don't overwork it.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.880
Probably the biggest mistake made is overworking it.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.500
And you work it 'til it's dead.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.680
Then you just, you have a big old cotton ball

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.700
laid up there in the sky.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:49.030
Very gently, very gently.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:52.810
All you're doing is grazing it.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:55.150
Barely go across.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.380
Okay, and that's how we make a little cloud.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.000
And there's many, many ways of making clouds.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.680
This is probably one of the simplest and most effective.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:11.400
Okay, got to make some decisions now.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.730
What are we going to have in here?

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.320
Maybe we'll put a little mountain over here.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:19.360
Now let's take some Prussian blue, some Van Dyke brown,

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.600
and a little bit of alizarin crimson.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.100
And mix them all together.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.190
Pick your paint up and turn it over.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.390
That assures that you'll mix it all.

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:30.000
Otherwise you won't mix what's against the pattern.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.260
So pick it up, turn it over, like so.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:36.050
Okay, now we'll take a little bit of paint on the knife.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:37.740
Let's go right up here.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.720
Maybe there's a little mountain that lives right here.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:48.600
Really, really pushing this paint into the fabric.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.890
Just like you're trying to push it right through the canvas.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:55.890
Now one of the questions that I hear quite frequently is,

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.960
"Do I always use a stretch canvas?"

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.610
I always do use a stretch canvas.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:08.630
If you use a canvas board, it will absorb your Magic White

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:12.440
and very rapidly you're working on a dry canvas.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.620
Creates unbelievable problems.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.720
I always use a canvas that is double primed,

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.490
has two coats of primer on it.

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:21.050
And that way the Magic White will stay wet

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:23.470
for extended periods of time.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.790
And that's what you're looking for.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.350
'Cause maybe you won't finish the painting today

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:29.140
and you wanna come back tomorrow and work on it.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:30.000
Some people don't paint

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.010
quite as fast as I do.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.320
And they want to come back and work on it.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.460
So your magic white will stay wet for several days.

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:42.120
Okay, we'll pull out, this is just titanium white.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:46.450
And let's put a little bit of snow up here on this mountain.

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:56.040
Barely, barely touching, just a whisper.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.010
Just let that knife literally, literally float

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.000
across the canvas.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:03.980
Maybe there's a little peak right there.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.900
That may be in the background.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:09.940
And you can make these as wide or as small as you want them.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.530
Just keep building them.

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.260
It's your mountain.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.180
So you do whatever you want to with it.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:19.440
It's your mountain.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:23.520
Okay, I'm gonna take a little Prussian blue and white,

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.560
just blue and white, and we'll make a shadow color.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.740
Okay, pull your paint out flat and then cut across

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:34.140
so you have a small roll of paint

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.450
right on the edge of the knife.

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:40.590
Okay, let's go up to the canvas, touch,

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.730
and just barely touch it and follow the angle.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:48.110
Now, notice the angle's opposite of the highlight.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:52.370
Highlight goes in one direction, shadow in the other.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.610
Very, very simple way to make little mountains

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.980
that are very effective and beautiful.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.860
And you need these shadows.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:06.750
That's the shadows, that's what separates these.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:09.490
If you don't have the shadows in the right places,

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:11.330
then your mountains won't look right.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:15.900
And every highlight needs its own private shadow.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:19.090
Doesn't have a shadow, it just lays there.

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:21.180
You need that shadow to push it up

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:26.480
to make it an individual.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:30.000
Now let's make some mist on the bottom of this mountain.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:34.910
Use just a clean, dry, 2 1/2 inch brush and just tap.

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:38.520
Follow the angles in your mountain.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.020
Always follow those angles.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:44.130
Mountains are nothing but geometric shapes.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:46.310
They're just games of angles.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.950
Study the angles.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:52.370
Lift upward, this removes the tap marks

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:54.960
and creates beautiful soft mist.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:56.800
That easy.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.520
I told you you could do it.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:05.980
Okay, let's have some fun, let's have some fun.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:08.570
Now we got us a nice little mountain in the background,

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:12.200
some beautiful clouds, so let's have some fun.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:15.010
I'm gonna go right into, there's some sap green,

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.270
and this is the mountain color,

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:20.830
so this is Van Dyke brown, Prussian blue, sap green,

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:22.920
and we'll throw some crimson in there too.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.920
A lot of paint on the brush,

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:27.530
pull that brush through the paint, bend it,

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:30.000
load a lot of paint, look at how it looks.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.200
Okay, now we're gonna put that rounded corner

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.600
to the top when we touch the canvas.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.010
There, you can see it very well.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.780
Okay, let's go up here.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.480
Maybe you gotta make some decisions.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:43.420
Maybe, maybe, maybe, right there.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:46.050
Right there lives the tree.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.820
There he is.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:48.880
And this is just background,

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.780
so you're not really concerned about anything

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:54.040
except just basic shapes.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:58.360
You know, just wherever you think there would be a tree.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.810
That's exactly where there were to be a tree.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:08.710
Okay, maybe, maybe, maybe, maybe.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.480
There.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.080
And start thinking about the general lay of the land here.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.780
Maybe this is gonna be coming downhill, so.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:19.530
Start planting that.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:24.360
And wherever you want a tree, drop him in.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:34.530
Begin working on all kinds of little basic shapes here.

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:35.610
But you're still paying attention

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:41.560
to the general lay of the land.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:42.850
Bigger bush.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:45.140
Push that mountain back a little further.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:46.880
When you're putting this in,

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:50.670
you don't want to kill the misty area

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:52.730
between the mountain and your background.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:54.540
If you kill this misty area,

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.760
it's gonna pull that mountain right up against this.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.090
And you want to keep some distance there

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:00.000
to make the mountain look like it's far, far away.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:02.380
So, leave this misty area.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.220
It's very, very important to you.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:06.550
Leave that.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:07.970
Okay, let me just go on here

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:14.590
and drop in a little bit more of this background.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:16.930
This is a super way just to practice, too,

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:19.220
is to really have nothing in your mind

00:12:19.220 --> 00:12:23.410
except a time of day and a time of year.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:24.510
Hit the canvas.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.380
Just let something happen.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:27.220
Bring it out of here.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:30.000
You don't have to trace and draw all these pictures

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:36.750
on there. It's in here. All you have to do is let it out, put it on that canvas. Maybe

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.790
we're gonna have a little pond right here. Watch how easy it is to make a reflection.

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:46.520
Let's go right in here. All we do is grab that and pull down. We want the pond to reflect

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:51.830
the color that's around it. So all you do is pick up some of this background color and

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:55.910
pull down. That easy.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:13:00.000
Reflections are one of the most fantastic things to do in this technique. Cause the canvas is

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.070
wet with the magic white, oh son of a gun.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:08.530
You can make unbelievable reflections.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.070
Now these lines should be straight across,

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:12.170
go straight across with them.

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:15.270
Don't want the water to run out on the floor.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:19.670
Okay, now then, let's put a few little trunks

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:21.270
here and there, we'll use a knife today.

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:26.220
I'll take some burnt umber, a little bit of white in it,

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:30.000
pull it out very flat, cut across so we got that small roll of

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.490
paint right out on the edge of the knife there.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:36.560
There you can see it, just a tiny bit, okay?

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.980
Now, all you gotta do is touch the canvas,

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:41.300
and the canvas will pull off what it wants.

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:42.800
If your trunk needs to be wider,

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.340
pull it to the side a little bit.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:48.060
But most of the time, all you have to do is just touch.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.860
And if you don't over mix your paint,

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:52.990
then it'll be marbled, and it'll,

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:54.390
all kinds of beautiful little things

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:55.550
will happen automatically.

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:58.390
You don't have to worry about it.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:13:59.730
You could set and mix up

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:03.300
a dozen different colors or you can mix your paint marbly

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:08.330
and let it happen, let it happen.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:11.900
We learn to use everything that happens.

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:14.650
That's what's so much fun about this.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.110
We talk about we don't make mistakes,

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:19.530
we have happy accidents, and that's true.

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:23.960
There's nothing that you can't fix very easily.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.490
Now let's put some highlights on this.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:30.000
And I'll get a one inch brush and let's go

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.240
I'm going to add a little bit of cad yellow

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:38.190
and some sap green, some sap green.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:45.240
There, okay, pull that brush through that paint.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:48.140
Pull it through, a lot of paint.

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:49.840
Okay, I'm gonna hold it up here and let you look at it.

